title: What Scarlett must now do differently.
pid: 55deb6cc-0d0d-48d7-9022-4df5e77d92db
body: |2-
  - She need not run the script: the pacer runs it after each session.
    Only an interactive session still going is behind; run it by hand
    for that.
  - To sum or compare across models, she should use 'weighted_usd',
    which is in dollars of Opus: a Fable list dollar counts 2.5, every
    other model's 1. 'usd' stays list price. Over everything so far,
    $318 at list price is $505 weighted.
  - To change a weight, she edits SUBSCRIPTION_WEIGHT_PER_LIST_DOLLAR at
    the top of the script and runs it; every row is reweighed, the rows
    of deleted transcripts too. Sonnet's and Haiku's 1 is her
    "everything else" rate, never measured apart.
  - 'mission_kind' (plan, reading, build or tending) is filled only for
    missions lent from now on; every row before is empty, so for those
    she still has to classify by hand.
  - For fitting the windows, she no longer reads transcripts:
    'data/claude/spending/requests.tsv' has one row per request with its
    'time' (when the response began to arrive, to the second), model,
    tokens, 'usd' and 'weighted_usd'; its 'id' is the account row's.
    The script's help ends with a query of the dollars between two of
    the pacer's log times, by specialist, that runs as written.
  - Two columns were inserted: 'mission_kind' after 'mission',
    'weighted_usd' after 'usd'. An awk command that counts columns
    ('$17' for 'usd') must count again.
